-- Pass 2.5 call-algebra fixture: a plain typed direct call.
-- `call.inline` must dispatch and the C must hold a direct `add(...)` with no
-- `lua_invoke` anywhere in the translation unit. The result is BOUND rather
-- than returned: a call in tail position dispatches the whole call algebra,
-- which would make the `@hot` discrimination in hot.id unfalsifiable.

add(a: i64, b: i64): i64
    a + b
end

main(): i64
    x = add(1, 2)
    x
end
